WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.935
-Margot and I are about
to face off in a game of

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:03.937
"Box of Lies."

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:04.937
Now...

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:06.272
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.707
...here's how it works.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:10.242
Upstage are a bunch
of boxes containing objects

00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:11.978
neither of us have seen before.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.747
Taking turns, we're going
to select a box

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.248
and open it on
our side of the table

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:16.916
out of view of the other person.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.651
You remove the object
from the box,

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.819
show it to the audience,

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.554
and then look at
your opponent and tell them

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.955
what's in your box.

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:25.625
They have to guess if you're
lying or telling the truth.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.026
We'll play it three rounds.

00:00:27.026 --> 00:00:28.795
Margot, why don't you pick
the first box?

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.930
-I go first?
-Yeah, please.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.331
You good at this?
-Mmm.

00:00:32.331 --> 00:00:35.435
-You good at lying?
-I'm a terrible liar, actually.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.537
Or is that a lie,
and I'm really good at this?

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.872
-Ooh!

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.439
That was sneaky already.
-I'm in your head, Jimmy.

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:41.541
I'm in your head.
-I know, yeah.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:43.943
Oh, oh, I can see
the box is a bit heavy.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.145
-It is.

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.145
-Yeah.
Oh, maybe not.

00:00:46.145 --> 00:00:47.914
Okay, good.
All right.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.649
-Hey, hey.
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.451
Ooh!
-Hey, hey, ooh?

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.219
-Saucy!

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:54.220
-Saucy?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.888
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.724
-It's kind of risqué for...
-Really?

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.559
-I mean, it is
a late night show.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.760
I'm sure that I...
-Risqué?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.161
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:04.597
Ooh! Oh!
-Really?

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:07.600
Saucy?
Something saucy on my show?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.301
Risqué?
-I mean, it's kind of sexy.

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:10.703
Like, I...

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.605
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.473
I mean...

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:16.509
You're kind of in it.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.111
-Okay?
-Um...

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.313
-Wow.
-...'cause it's your head,

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:27.619
and it's like the body of,
like, the red-dress lady,

00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:29.855
Jessica Rabbit.
Roger Rabbit?

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:31.490
Jessica Rabbit?
-Yeah, from "Roger Rabbit"?

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.460
-Yeah, it's your head...
-My head on...

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.828
-...and her body.
And you look great.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.264
-...Jessica Rabbit's body.
-You look good.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.300
-And I look good.
-You look great.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:47.674
-My head...
has never been in doll form.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.308
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.308 --> 00:01:50.576
-I mean...
-Really?

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:53.046
So it's my head?
Maybe someone made my head

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.081
and put on
a Jessica Rabbit body?

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.449
-It's a bobble-head sort of --
Like a bobble-head doll.

00:01:57.449 --> 00:02:00.019
-I did have a bobble-head done.
-Oh, you did?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:01.387
-Yeah.
-Right, well, here it is.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.389
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:05.558
-Yeah, but the bobble-head's
a giant head.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.827
It would have to be
a giant Jessica Rabbit.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.096
I don't know if
that's just physically...

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.499
-It looks good.
I think it looks good.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.034
-Oh, yeah yeah yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.502
See, right there, you just...
-They should sell this.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.837
-...you just busted yourself.

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:20.072
I think... you lie!

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:21.941
-[ Laughing ] I did.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:23.543
-You did?

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.845
[ Ding ]
Oh, is that a lobster?

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.879
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:28.414
Oh, that was
actually pretty good!

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.082
-[ Laughs ]
-That was very good!

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:32.017
I was like, "Wait, it's not much
to do with that lobster."

00:02:32.017 --> 00:02:33.219
-Okay, here we go.
-It was like a red thing.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:35.020
-No, you're very good.
What am I looking for?

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.723
[ Audience shouting ]

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:38.624
No problem, here we go.
-Do I put the box down?

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:39.792
-Oh, sure.
-Okay.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.227
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:42.795
-[ Grunting ]

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.764
-Oh, come on.
-[ Grunting ]

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:47.567
-Please.
-[ Grunting ]

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.002
-I'm not falling for this trick.
-Oh!

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:52.405
Oh, my back!
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:54.407
-My back is killing me, oh.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.576
Oh, saucy!
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.111
-Saucy?

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.412
-Yeah.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.780
Saucy.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:08.554
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.089
-That sexy, huh?

00:03:10.089 --> 00:03:14.460
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.364
-I don't know
what to make of this!

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.299
-I'm very familiar with this.

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:23.336
-Okay.
-It's -- It's ice cream...

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.904
-Oh.
-...in a --

00:03:25.904 --> 00:03:28.774
Looks like a Houston Astros hat,
like baseball hat,

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.342
upside-down baseball hat.

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:33.646
But interesting enough,
they have a Trump hair --

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.848
It looks like Trump hair
is sprinkled on top.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:39.552
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:42.121
-Just wanna recap. Um...
-Yeah, no problem.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.657
-There's ice cream?
-Ice cream in a plastic,

00:03:45.657 --> 00:03:49.062
upside-down baseball cap.

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:53.565
-I'm gonna say that's a lie.

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:55.234
-Gosh, you're so right.
-Yes!

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.103
[ Ding ]

00:03:57.103 --> 00:04:00.139
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.641
I didn't know what to do.
I don't even know --

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.443
That's so bizarre, I didn't know
how to make anything up right.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:05.445
-That is really bizarre.
-This is the --

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.279
This is the tie-breaker
right here.

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:09.314
Whoever wins the next round
wins the whole thing.

00:04:09.314 --> 00:04:11.350
-I hate losing to you, Jimmy.
I don't want to lose.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.619
-No, hey, I won't let
you lose unless you do.

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:16.522
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.190
All right, all right.
You choose --

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.559
You choose the box
in this one.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.559
Audience, which...

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:27.433
[ Audience shouting ]

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.268
-That's my favorite number,
so I'm gonna go with it.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:30.869
-All right, yeah.
Do you like two?

00:04:30.869 --> 00:04:32.205
-Yeah.
-Is that your birthday?

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:33.739
-Yeah, I'm born on the 2nd.
How original.

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.374
-Hey, no, I like that.

00:04:35.374 --> 00:04:38.777
-Ooh!
Actually, kind of heavy.

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:41.313
-All right.
That kind of sounded heavy, too.

00:04:41.313 --> 00:04:42.915
So, here we go.
[ Suspenseful music plays ]

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.316
Oh, thank you, Roots.

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:47.152
Now they're playing music.
Now I can't hear anything.

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:48.154
-[ Laughs ]
-All right.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:49.989
This is all part of the thing.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:53.492
All right, I'm looking
at your reaction.

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:54.494
-Oh.

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:57.196
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.165
It's a, uh...

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.266
-Would I have this
on my desk at work?

00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:02.468
-Most probably.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.503
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:07.272
I think most people would have
it, like, on their desk.

00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:08.607
[ Cheers ]

00:05:08.607 --> 00:05:10.443
-Don't play!
Don't play along, please.

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.178
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.446
-Be on my side.
-All right.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:16.015
What is it, what is it?
-It's kind of like a --

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.383
This is why it could be
on your desk.

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.352
You could use it
as a paperweight.

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.153
-Okay.

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:24.490
-But you probably wouldn't,
but you could if you wanted to.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:28.995
It's kind of like a dish,
like a salad-y,

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:31.297
glass crystal-y ball.
-Uh-huh.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:35.134
-Um, and...

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.636
It's filled with Band-Aids,
so that's kind of gross.

00:05:37.636 --> 00:05:38.771
So you wouldn't have
that on your desk.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:39.972
-No, yeah yeah yeah.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.440
Like, open Band-Aids?

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.109
-No, they're just like
the Band-Aid packets.

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:47.179
-Okay.
-And then, there's, like,

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:50.716
a little toy car
just sitting on the top.

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:51.884
I don't know what it's doing.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.520
Yeah.
-You kind of lost

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.222
your accent a little bit
describing it.

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:57.589
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.589 --> 00:06:01.627
So, that makes me think that --
You'd be like,

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:04.062
[ Cockney accent ] "There's a
Band-Aid in a bowl -- in a bowl,

00:06:04.062 --> 00:06:05.097
a paperweight."

00:06:05.097 --> 00:06:06.098
-[ Cockney accent ]
A paperweight.

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:07.099
-[ Normal voice ]
You didn't say...

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:08.401
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:13.806
You said, "It's a Band-Aid
in a, uh, A-O-O-A-O-A-O!"

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.875
Oh, I'm gonna say you lie!

00:06:15.875 --> 00:06:17.410
-Yes, I lied.
-Yes!

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.744
Oh, my God!
[ Ding ]

00:06:18.744 --> 00:06:19.745
What was it?

00:06:19.745 --> 00:06:21.280
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.149
Oh, it's Nicholas Cage
on an egg in a bird!

00:06:24.149 --> 00:06:26.151
-Is it Nicholas Cage?
-I think it's Nicholas Cage.

00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:27.587
I have no idea.
I think it's Nicholas Cage.

00:06:27.587 --> 00:06:29.321
Margot Robbie, either way,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:06:29.321 --> 00:06:31.256
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.256 --> 00:06:32.258
Thank you for playing.
-Thank you.

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:34.227
I'm glad you won
-[ Laughing ] I love it.

